@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Local evaluation without publication
+
+Use `/coding-agent:analyze "<requirement>" --type bugfix --evaluation-only`
+in a dedicated isolated project clone. This opt-in supports local full bugfix
+pipelines in auto mode. It rejects review/release/feature, Jira intake and
+`--auto-merge`. Existing tickets/default publish behavior are unchanged;
+`auto_merge=false` by itself still permits PR creation.
+
+Before dispatch, intake writes config.publication_policy=evaluation_only and
+runs scripts/publication_policy.py --workspace <absolute-workspace> --repo
+<absolute-repo> --init. This exclusively creates publication-policy.json,
+binding ticket, repo, workspace, source base and auto mode. The lock is not
+replaced on resume. Policy/identity changes are rejected by Write/Edit guards.
+
+At EVALUATION_PASS the orchestrator runs the same CLI with --finalize instead
+of pushing or creating a PR. It checks completed pipeline stages and plan steps,
+the existing oracle completion and applied candidate-selection gates, the
+nonempty evaluation report and clean tracked subject source. Existing oracle
+tier rules still govern permitted ChainBench/regression skips; required stage
+FAIL/missing, e2e skips, unresolved oracle/selection and stale evidence fail.
+The CLI writes evaluation-exit.json before atomically replacing state.json with
+EVALUATED. COMPLETION/PR delivery stays unperformed. Exit is local evaluation,
+not independent quality, human acceptance or publication authorization.
+
+The receipt binds state, HEAD/tree, runner and workspace evidence hashes. Append
+telemetry logs/impl.log and logs/agent-transcript.jsonl are excluded so the host's
+final PostToolUse Agent event remains recorded; those logs are not exit gate
+evidence. Other modified/added/deleted evidence, source and state invalidate it.
+Use --check-exit on resume. An interrupted receipt without the terminal state
+is not completion; recover any leftover state.next.json explicitly before retry.
+
+Stop prioritizes the newest locked evaluation workspace in this isolated repo.
+A valid EVALUATED receipt allows repeated stops without publication re-entry.
+An incomplete or invalid boundary requests evaluation/diagnosis or BLOCKED,
+never publication. BLOCKED stops locally. stop_hook_active allows the host to
+stop after its single continuation; that flag never proves evaluation passed.
+The lock remains effective after the old freshness window and after local exit.
+Another ticket's auto_merge flag cannot relax it.
+
+PreToolUse publication-guard covers known git push/send-email, gh PR/release/API,
+common transfer/deploy command spellings and MCP outside CKS/ChainBench/read-only
+Jira. Direct policy/receipt Write/Edit is denied. It is a finite tool guard,
+not a shell interpreter or an outbound-network sandbox: scripts, aliases,
+encoded commands, direct file writes, arbitrary programs and host bypasses are
+not comprehensively prevented. No caller identity is authenticated by hashes.
+Use restricted host tools/MCP/network permissions; actual host event dispatch
+and outbound isolation still need separate validation. Do not run evaluation
+and unrelated publishing tasks together in this clone. To publish later, use
+an explicitly authorized new workflow/clone; do not downgrade this ticket.
+
+Controlled tests execute real oracle/selection fixtures and hook subprocesses.
+Fixture panel opinions are not independent review. No model calls, external
+PR/Jira mutations or installed-host session is needed for these tests.
